  _id: 14041209
  _key: DIALOGUE_SERAPHINE_NODE_SIGIL_REVELATION
  _displayName: 
  _description: 
  _speakerName: Seraphine
  _dialogueSegments:
  - That Sigil bears the mark of the First Flame's guardians.
  - My order once entrusted such relics to the sanctuaries. They were symbols of
    our duty, reminders that the Flame belonged to the world, not to any one guardian.
  - 'I once believed that duty would endure forever.

    But one among us tried
    to preserve the Flame by his own strength... and paid a terrible price.'
  - 'His name was Aurelian.

    He was my brother.'
  _dialogueText: 'That Sigil bears the mark of the First Flame''s guardians.

    My
    order once entrusted such relics to the sanctuaries. They were symbols of our
    duty, reminders that the Flame belonged to the world, not to any one guardian.

    I
    once believed that duty would endure forever.

    But one among us tried to
    preserve the Flame by his own strength... and paid a terrible price.

    His
    name was Aurelian.

    He was my brother.'
  _choices:
  - _choiceText: Tell me about Aurelian.
